pnpm is a fast, disk space efficient package manager for Node.js.  Packages
are stored once in a content-addressable store and linked into each project's
node_modules, so repeated dependencies are not duplicated on disk.  It uses a
strict, non-flat node_modules layout that only exposes declared dependencies,
and supports workspaces for monorepos.

This port installs the 10.x release line, the last pure-JavaScript major, run
through the node22 interpreter.
